00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:17.040
Did it soak in?

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:19.240
It's my own special mix!

00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:20.470
Traitor!

00:02:20.630 --> 00:02:22.230
Wh-What?!

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:24.390
All I did was help her put the ointment on!

00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:26.320
I'm not talking about this!

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:27.610
Then what ARE you talking about?

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:29.530
Think about what happened the other day!

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:32.190
What?

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:35.540
I don't care if you put the ointment on my back.

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:37.890
Shizuka-sensei doesn't have to be the one to do it.

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:39.170
...okay?

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:40.960
Just get out.

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:42.880
Huh? That was abrupt.

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:46.870
My boobs hurt because of how you shot that gun!

00:02:47.270 --> 00:02:48.870
I'm going to put ointment on my chest by myself!

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:57.610
She needs to lighten up...{"How carefree..." from manga for flow -A0}

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:01.010
Dumbass!

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:03.300
It fell 'cuz you're walking too fast!

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:06.880
I'll help!

00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:08.540
Oh, it's okay.

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:10.650
Let the adults do this.

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:12.390
Adults?

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:15.160
You kids can sit back and relax!

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:16.900
What?

00:03:17.890 --> 00:03:19.490
Do not be so concerned.

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:27.010
Is something wrong?

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:30.800
Uh, no.

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:33.450
You look good in that.

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:35.170
Like, really good.

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:41.340
Uh, I...

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:42.990
I wasn't trying to be weird!

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:45.930
Oh, no! I did not think of it like that.

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:53.780
Huh? What's going on?

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:57.630
Why're you in a good mood?

00:03:58.810 --> 00:04:01.730
We were telling each other how nice it is to see you happy, Alice.

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:04.480
Yeah! I'm happy!

00:04:11.910 --> 00:04:12.790
Hang in there, 'kay?

00:04:14.930 --> 00:04:18.470
Yeah I know! You're ALWAYS right!

00:04:19.010 --> 00:04:19.710
Takagi?

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:23.040
Takagi, what's up?

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:27.050
Didn't I tell you to use my first name?

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:29.900
Oh, yeah. Sorry.

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:32.200
Don't lower your head all the time! You're a man!

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:35.930
Well, whatever.

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:37.340
You're fine now.

00:04:37.820 --> 00:04:38.650
Just you.

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:41.740
Ta—... er, Sa—

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:42.570
Enough!

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:44.950
What was that?

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:48.650
She's troubling you, isn't she?

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:53.770
Oh, no.

00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:56.740
You've gotten used to her?

00:04:57.690 --> 00:04:59.600
You have been friends since kindergarten.

00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:05.400
Naw, uh... Anyway, cool place you got here.

00:05:06.210 --> 00:05:11.070
I always knew your house was nice, but not this nice.

00:05:11.980 --> 00:05:14.550
Oh, you've never been here before, have you?

00:05:15.140 --> 00:05:16.870
Eh, well...

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:19.230
You were afraid, weren't you?

00:05:19.470 --> 00:05:21.260
Uh, well...

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:23.460
Sorry.

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:25.840
I like honest men.

00:05:26.750 --> 00:05:29.970
Anyway, we don't want to overstay our welcome.

00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:35.700
Here's the carrier... spring... ejector...

00:05:37.490 --> 00:05:39.300
Sounds like you're enjoying yourself.

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:44.520
Better enjoy it while you can.

00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:46.870
It's not like we can stay here forever.

00:05:47.540 --> 00:05:49.070
Why not, Takagi-san?{Added "-san" -A0}

00:05:49.590 --> 00:05:51.590
If we stay here at this stronghold of a mansion...

00:05:51.630 --> 00:05:55.870
You didn't think about how difficult it is to secure water and electricity?

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:57.960
We learn about those things in grade school.

00:05:59.260 --> 00:06:00.990
So basically...

00:06:01.450 --> 00:06:04.220
In order to keep that huge network running,

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:10.000
you need a well-organized 
and countless number of specialists

00:06:10.350 --> 00:06:12.530
who feel safe and can work with ease.

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:16.590
When the dead began attacking,

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:20.990
the Commander sent the SDF to the power plants on his own.{Capitalized "Commander" -A0}

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:25.880
He couldn't wait for those
foolish prime ministers to move.

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:29.820
But in that case, maintaining them...

00:06:30.230 --> 00:06:35.630
I wonder how long those operators can continue maintaining the plants?

00:06:36.970 --> 00:06:38.550
They have family too.

00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:42.090
And their families aren't there
with them at the power plants.

00:06:42.520 --> 00:06:44.280
So you're going to use those buses?

00:06:45.010 --> 00:06:47.730
Yes. Only those who we are responsible...

00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:54.120
No, we will bring only those who are prepared to survive.

00:06:57.020 --> 00:06:57.920
Hey. hey!{"Woah" -A0}

00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:01.220
Hey there little buddy. Isn't that real?

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:03.820
That's not something a kid should be playing with.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:08.040
Is that all, Mato-san?{"Maddo" to "Mato" -A0}

00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:10.220
Oh, Saya-sama. {W.E.: I really think "Miss Saya" would've sounded better than "Milady Saya" here.}

00:07:10.890 --> 00:07:15.810
Uh, no. I came to tell you that I'm done fixing up that car you came here in.

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:18.260
I see. Thank you.

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:24.520
You really are like a princess! Pretty cool! {WE: Is "pretty cool" the new "fabulous" or something?}{"from a good family" to "like a princess" -A0}

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:27.210
I don't want to hear you say that.

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:30.340
Anyway, you better do something about that!

00:07:31.620 --> 00:07:32.970
But... why?

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:35.280
You didn't understand his reaction just now?

00:07:36.170 --> 00:07:38.180
The majority of the people here are adults!

00:07:38.730 --> 00:07:41.310
What do we mean to them?

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:46.730
I think we should discuss this with the rest of the gang.

00:07:48.840 --> 00:07:50.690
<i>I want her to understand.{Italics added -A0}</i>

00:07:51.560 --> 00:07:54.360
<i>But she won't understand no matter what I tell her.{Italics added -A0}</i>

00:07:55.510 --> 00:07:57.950
<i>I wonder if I can ask you to do it?{Italics added -A0}</i>

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:01.080
Persuade Takagi?

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:05.110
I've never won an argument with her since kindergarten.

00:08:10.600 --> 00:08:13.490
Do we really have to gather in here?

00:08:13.750 --> 00:08:16.920
Well, you can't move. I don't think we have a choice.

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:20.130
So what do we need to talk about?

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:24.810
Whether we're going to stay as companions or not.{"stick with this group" to "stay as companions"-nakama -A0}

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:28.360
Companions? {"This group" to "Companions" -A0}

00:08:30.020 --> 00:08:31.190
Of course.

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:37.810
As of now, we have become part of
 a much larger and more powerful group.

00:08:38.650 --> 00:08:39.180
So basically...

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:42.390
Right. We have two options.

00:08:43.730 --> 00:08:44.890
We can join them.

00:08:45.380 --> 00:08:46.450
Or we can go our own way.

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:49.990
But do we really need to split from them?

00:08:51.100 --> 00:08:53.070
I mean, the streets have gotten worse.

00:08:53.690 --> 00:08:55.360
Your dad has this under control.{lit: your dad is skillful. you figure out what this means in this situation. i think it refers to how he's handling the situation.}

00:08:56.360 --> 00:08:58.690
It must run in the family.

00:08:59.460 --> 00:09:00.800
Your mom is something else, too.

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:03.380
Yeah, she really is.

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:05.240
I was always proud of her.{"used to be" to "was always" -A0}

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:09.360
I still am now.

00:09:09.950 --> 00:09:12.260
She did all this in two days.

00:09:13.600 --> 00:09:15.600
But... she could've...

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:17.020
Takagi!

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:18.410
Use my first name!

00:09:19.670 --> 00:09:21.440
Don't talk about your parents like that.

00:09:22.110 --> 00:09:25.790
Now's not the time for that. 
This has been hard on everyone.

00:09:25.890 --> 00:09:27.970
You sound like my mom!

00:09:29.140 --> 00:09:30.130
I know!

00:09:30.510 --> 00:09:33.340
I know that my parents are the best!{"the cream of the crop!" to "the best! -A0}

00:09:33.610 --> 00:09:35.590
When they realized that
something strange was going on,{"fishy" to "strange" -A0}

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:39.440
they immediately took action and protected 
their mansion, their subordinates, and their families!

00:09:39.530 --> 00:09:42.680
They're amazing! Really, really amazing!

00:09:43.360 --> 00:09:46.010
I mean, it's not like they forgot about their daughter!

00:09:46.330 --> 00:09:48.570
In fact, I was the first thing on their minds!

00:09:48.820 --> 00:09:49.430
Hey, that's kinda—

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:51.680
I wouldn't think any less of them!

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:53.990
My mom and dad are really something else!

00:09:54.440 --> 00:09:57.640
They didn't think I could survive,
 so they just gave up on me right away!

00:09:57.770 --> 00:09:58.850
Stop it, Saya!{"Shut up" to "Stop it" -A0}

00:10:03.280 --> 00:10:03.920
Komuro-kun?

00:10:06.520 --> 00:10:08.950
What? You just...

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:10.950
But... you finally...

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:14.820
Takashi...

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:17.900
It's not just you! It's the same for me!

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:20.330
It's the same for all of us!

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:25.590
Actually, you're better off than the rest of us! 
You know your parents are safe!

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:27.400
Much better!

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:42.490
Okay, I get it.

00:10:42.930 --> 00:10:44.330
I get it. Let me go.

00:10:52.470 --> 00:10:53.470
My bad.

00:10:54.170 --> 00:10:57.840
Yeah, really. But whatever.

00:10:59.430 --> 00:11:02.910
If we don't get down to business...

00:11:15.810 --> 00:11:16.520
Is that...?

00:11:16.740 --> 00:11:17.490
Yes.

00:11:17.740 --> 00:11:21.520
That's the former head of Tokonosu 
and current head of the Takagi family.

00:11:24.810 --> 00:11:28.050
That's a man who does everything as he sees fit.{WE: see fits -> sees fit}

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:34.380
That's my papa!

00:11:47.180 --> 00:11:50.170
This man's name is... Doi Tetsutaro!

00:11:51.800 --> 00:11:54.910
He used to be a retainer of the Takagi family.

00:11:55.000 --> 00:11:56.700
He is also my best friend.

00:11:59.460 --> 00:12:00.580
And today,

00:12:01.340 --> 00:12:03.070
in the midst of a rescue,

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:06.740
he was bitten while helping his comrades!

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:14.220
Self-sacrifice is the most noble act we humans are capable of doing!

00:12:14.690 --> 00:12:15.470
But...

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:18.070
He is no longer human.

00:12:18.190 --> 00:12:21.200
He died and turned into a very dangerous <i>thing!</i>

00:12:24.990 --> 00:12:26.370
Thus...

00:12:28.570 --> 00:12:30.120
Here...

00:12:31.760 --> 00:12:36.300
I shall carry out my duty 
as a man of the Takagi family!

00:12:43.800 --> 00:12:45.790
I'm sorry, my child...

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:12.690
This is our reality!

00:13:13.900 --> 00:13:16.770
Whether they were a good friend, beloved family members,

00:13:17.360 --> 00:13:20.510
or a former lover, you must be ready to kill them!

00:13:22.310 --> 00:13:25.790
If you wish to live, you must fight!

00:13:44.080 --> 00:13:45.150
What's the matter, Hirano?

00:13:45.830 --> 00:13:46.850
You don't look too good.

00:13:47.690 --> 00:13:49.770
Swords aren't efficient enough...

00:13:50.800 --> 00:13:51.790
Wh-What?

00:13:52.360 --> 00:13:54.150
I said they aren't efficient enough!

00:13:54.560 --> 00:13:56.820
If the blade of a Japanese sword hits bone, it'll break!

00:13:56.960 --> 00:13:59.540
It's useless after three kills!

00:14:00.110 --> 00:14:01.970
You assume too much, Hirano-kun.

00:14:02.900 --> 00:14:06.790
Even in swordsmanship, results come in numbers.

00:14:08.060 --> 00:14:09.110
The skill of the swordsman,

00:14:09.430 --> 00:14:10.380
the quality of the sword,

00:14:10.960 --> 00:14:12.760
and the strength of the heart.

00:14:13.910 --> 00:14:16.520
If the three of those are high-level enough,

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:19.900
your fighting prowess shall not dwindle,
 no matter how many you kill.

00:14:20.170 --> 00:14:22.860
B-But if blood gets...

00:14:22.960 --> 00:14:25.290
Hey, Hirano. That's enough.

00:14:25.470 --> 00:14:26.700
Don't touch me!

00:14:27.240 --> 00:14:28.330
Don't get in my way!

00:14:28.510 --> 00:14:30.350
You can't even fire a gun!

00:14:31.090 --> 00:14:33.360
Cool it, Hirano!

00:14:35.260 --> 00:14:36.400
Hey, Hirano!

00:14:41.430 --> 00:14:43.880
Two sides of the same coin?

00:14:46.730 --> 00:14:47.590
Onii-chan!

00:14:50.360 --> 00:14:53.140
Did you and Kouta-chan get in an argument?

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:55.640
Maybe...

00:14:56.090 --> 00:14:58.080
No, I guess we did.{"Yeah" to "No" -A0}

00:14:58.400 --> 00:15:01.080
Okay, I'll tell you something that'll cheer you up!

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:04.110
Talk to him again!

00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:08.420
Talk to him until you understand each other!

00:15:09.400 --> 00:15:10.920
You think I can do it?

00:15:11.320 --> 00:15:12.500
You can!

